    name="2 Data Standardization and Integration Value Stream"
    id="id-52e430553faa4e57ba91b46322485f30"
    documentation="Purpose:&#xD;&#xA;To transform raw, heterogeneous input data into a harmonized and interoperable structure that can be processed and compared consistently across domains and time.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Description:&#xD;&#xA;This value stream covers all activities related to syntactic and semantic standardization, coding, validation, and metadata alignment. Its goal is to ensure interoperability and comparability while preserving informational content. Data is mapped to standardized classifications, code lists, and statistical concepts defined in frameworks such as GSIM or SDMX.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The output artefact is a standardized dataset, ready for statistical editing and analysis. The primary value created is semantic coherence — the assurance that data from multiple sources can be used consistently across processes and domains.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Key capabilities: Data Harmonization, Metadata Management, Validation &amp; Conformance Checking, Classification Management, Reference Data Governance."
    viewpoint="value_stream">
